{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>An everlasting decree.</b> Even if he emerged from the immersion pool having been purified from severe impurity — HaShem enacted a decree, and therefore it was necessary to state it a second time. <b>And they shall not die</b> — this teaches that if they did not wash, even though they had emerged from immersion, they are subject to the death penalty and immersion does not avail."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:35.650581810Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}